## Notices for users

Flashing a custom kernel or boot image can permanently brick a device, and on
Xiaomi/Qualcomm phones an anti-rollback (ARB) fuse makes some downgrades
irreversible. The skills in this repository describe procedures that carry real
risk. You are responsible for backing up your own device and for understanding
what each command does before you run it.

Nothing in this repository ships code from Qualcomm, Xiaomi, Google, the Linux
kernel, AnyKernel3, KernelSU or any other upstream project. The skills only
describe how to build, package and flash software you obtain yourself; the
upstream licenses of those projects still govern their own code.
